course: dictionary
lesson: 1707
title: Cigarette: a word in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cigarette is a thin paper tube filled with dried tobacco that people light and smoke. The words around a new word give you clues. «Cigarettes, vapes and alcohol harm a growing body.» Harm means hurt or damage, so the sentence tells you that cigarettes are bad for your body.
explain: Some words have a slang version. «"Fags" is British slang for cigarettes» tells you that fags is an informal, everyday word for the same thing. Slang is relaxed language that a group of people use when they talk to each other.
explain: The sentence list gives more clues: «Cigarettes contain tobacco and nicotine; smoking causes lung disease, heart disease and cancer.» Tobacco and nicotine are the things inside a cigarette, and the illnesses show why adults and doctors warn about them. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A cigarette is a thin paper tube filled with dried tobacco.
fact: Cigarettes contain nicotine, which is addictive, so it can be very hard to stop once you start.
fact: Cigarette smoke harms other people nearby too; this is called second-hand smoke.
fact: Selling cigarettes to children is illegal.
fact: «Fags» is British slang for cigarettes, and a nicotine patch gives the body a little nicotine without the smoke to make quitting easier.
exercise: «Cigarettes, vapes and alcohol harm a growing body.» What does harm mean here? | *Hurt or damage | Help and feed | Make bigger | Make warm
exercise: «"Fags" is British slang for cigarettes.» What is slang? | A kind of medicine | Official words used in law | A type of tobacco | *Informal, everyday words used by a group of people
exercise: What is a cigarette? | *A thin paper tube filled with dried tobacco that people light and smoke | A small metal box for coins | A wooden stick used to light a fire | A glass bottle for medicine
test: «A nicotine patch gives the body a little nicotine without the smoke to make quitting easier.» What does quitting mean here? | Starting a new hobby | Tidying up a room | Running very fast | *Stopping something, such as smoking
test: Which harm does second-hand smoke cause? | Only to the smoker | *It harms other people breathing nearby | It makes the room warmer | It helps people breathe better
exam: «Cigarettes contain nicotine, which is addictive.» What does addictive mean? | Makes you sleepy | Makes you grow taller | Easy to give up | *Makes you want it so much that it is very hard to stop
